#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096390 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "a30b523c-d689-520a-a708-f3b5190eaf9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-477" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "872b9d99-ea39-540f-af2e-acbfa28186b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-478" :question/problem "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "d7c09fca-2f4b-5a0a-b687-938527b44d62" :question/math-academy-id "e-479" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096393 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/id #uuid "14ab2251-66fc-5f94-9821-f14fcc2c03e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-480" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72725af8-4242-5f4e-9756-310d26d4cbe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302951} {:answer/id #uuid "2118736a-61f5-544f-b3ef-ecbe4bff3a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302952} {:answer/id #uuid "18e3cd71-98de-509e-ad4e-0c9d7f4fe6f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302953} {:answer/id #uuid "8b0c2a01-fe89-5b2d-9b7d-aee915f17c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302954} {:answer/id #uuid "01e72d29-da06-53d7-8989-f238e92cbdbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01e72d29-da06-53d7-8989-f238e92cbdbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302955} :answer-field/id #uuid "70aa98f3-ddfc-5d05-ac4a-1fc1f7b322d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31a511c9-f158-5a66-beb5-cb2de94b5490" :question/math-academy-id "q-10565" :question/problem "$\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4({sec}^{2}⁡x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4{sec}^{2}⁡x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (-3{x}^{2}+4{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302956 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92e717c3-1802-5914-b7dc-3a561d667a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302958} {:answer/id #uuid "44a42067-0b76-5be8-ad9f-10f653942532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302959} {:answer/id #uuid "8e86a532-641e-593c-8ba1-1b9b33a5c7b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302960} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9067b1-fcbe-57a9-bb03-88132fe2d372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302961} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf2e10b-e1d2-5090-9a10-b0e940a76022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc9067b1-fcbe-57a9-bb03-88132fe2d372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302961} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1c42c27-0409-5092-81dc-3cbe6a9f5edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f82c9c40-c837-59db-b9bc-4010d9750009" :question/math-academy-id "q-114350" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡x=1-{cos}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({csc}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2becc949-0d22-5b2b-8888-b94b37dcad87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302965} {:answer/id #uuid "fb779127-1a42-5e05-8c8f-4fb06000a00b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302966} {:answer/id #uuid "e9606980-588e-59ae-a284-87eefb4c9d90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302967} {:answer/id #uuid "99bb938a-162a-55e1-83a2-5fb5fcf0c9de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302968} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc6b6de-09cf-5de7-92ce-e831b1af9117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cc6b6de-09cf-5de7-92ce-e831b1af9117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302969} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c639125-e644-5c95-9d82-47bd8aa00c97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "370be9f0-0eac-53fe-8b00-728cbe5bfa2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-114353" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b067803-e356-59ab-b56a-815759d59f7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302972} {:answer/id #uuid "2759eceb-a311-5908-8801-d68d919706d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302973} {:answer/id #uuid "152fb2d4-ee5a-518f-9a22-e7350d93decf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302974} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0c1e4a-0d81-5dc3-b7ef-67ae2278f12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302975} {:answer/id #uuid "8e604a39-c5f4-5995-a4ab-4d0963ea48b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a0c1e4a-0d81-5dc3-b7ef-67ae2278f12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302975} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bca70f5-3474-50a1-9aae-c870451900ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90f43e47-681b-5a78-9983-d0ba65d64a48" :question/math-academy-id "q-114423" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b081bbe0-f271-500e-8c58-531d3b64e372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302979} {:answer/id #uuid "10dec266-73ee-5d09-982d-ca8f1e21272e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302980} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca0a295-2e04-58f5-b605-f58721b4a899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302981} {:answer/id #uuid "6df78d83-aa18-5e16-b7fb-4f1b761885c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302982} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c80570-f736-56ac-b8c9-4ffdbfb59dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6df78d83-aa18-5e16-b7fb-4f1b761885c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302982} :answer-field/id #uuid "90b561d7-1ab3-5ed5-8e23-a038e6363ff8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38766e50-1265-5daf-a576-57dfb7a41e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-114435" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76c4721c-608a-5b2a-af63-3ea73948552b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302986} {:answer/id #uuid "94ce70e0-bbfc-5cfb-8df4-695beef43819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\pi -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302987} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1e20c1-367f-54d1-9c7f-d9c5b1cc5f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302988} {:answer/id #uuid "007bfff3-34a7-579f-a25f-80d37398e51e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302989} {:answer/id #uuid "88325cef-8b8f-5608-b88d-f5b0c6eb25e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e1e20c1-367f-54d1-9c7f-d9c5b1cc5f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302988} :answer-field/id #uuid "04fa0f23-46cd-5fe1-b915-ef4ed4a82b2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cc471bfe-2073-582d-86e5-26346f0a6a82" :question/math-academy-id "q-114441" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-x){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =[-0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ecd9746-ed07-53dd-9523-a872681c8a45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302993} {:answer/id #uuid "35c7d8e3-ba8b-56c6-9d0a-ef82bffb261b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302994} {:answer/id #uuid "6516a686-b959-5f41-ae89-9f1e68dd85a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302995} {:answer/id #uuid "4a19e8c6-0aaf-568b-ae01-791d7ce4c460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302996} {:answer/id #uuid "c9da0f4f-7651-5639-8054-d5bbf2c76bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a19e8c6-0aaf-568b-ae01-791d7ce4c460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302996} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a4a2baf-9ecf-5b5a-bd73-e41e7081a5da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3e210758-24a8-5827-bba0-96fda9d3e632" :question/math-academy-id "q-114469" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})={sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{[{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+1]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd8a96a2-63ed-54f6-9b16-adaa7d19756a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303000} {:answer/id #uuid "357509ba-03f5-58f4-9788-202afde1646a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303001} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7e1298-551f-5fb5-8473-de84e7dc33d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303002} {:answer/id #uuid "593b62b3-980f-5a45-87e3-e9b1f8053e68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303003} {:answer/id #uuid "de52dfe8-e93e-5581-a91b-8757a254d03b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "593b62b3-980f-5a45-87e3-e9b1f8053e68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303003} :answer-field/id #uuid "11413151-b4cb-5eec-8fee-0cebfdbb8679" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "00ef3dc6-530a-55c9-8a1b-bc6f728f1e6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114510" :question/problem "Determine $\\int \\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =5x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)={csc}^{2}⁡(5x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{[{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)+1]\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{csc}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡(5x-2)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)\\text{d}x & = \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bace1ab-1f8b-564a-965f-6880a8a258e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bace1ab-1f8b-564a-965f-6880a8a258e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288280} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd544d3-dbff-5f3e-8c77-9b66d9c3f746" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66b34e07-5d41-5462-a3f4-96722a374f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-346546" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14\\cdot 1-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(14x-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[14\\pi -\\frac{5}{3}{\\pi }^{3}]-[14\\cdot 0-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}] \\\\  & =14\\pi -\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e80eadc-14bc-57f6-ad26-c06bcfe326b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{4}+\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303007} {:answer/id #uuid "0b91961a-db58-56cf-9b3c-33a00726aef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b91961a-db58-56cf-9b3c-33a00726aef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303008} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eb0f959-b12a-5f80-8c44-36c534ca9ca4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79cb7490-7c08-5175-a41e-d3e420d4c759" :question/math-academy-id "q-352709" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}({cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}({cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-x)\\,{|}_{1}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =({(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-({1}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a474c54-9a2c-5453-89fd-c2257bcf7595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a474c54-9a2c-5453-89fd-c2257bcf7595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288297} :answer-field/id #uuid "9298b7c0-47e2-5a26-9926-01bbe7ab3f29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "844ead48-86d3-5441-9336-ed5d8fea3ef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-352714" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})={sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f04e7b64-6310-5158-a90f-913f675f7d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f04e7b64-6310-5158-a90f-913f675f7d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303011} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7f9b450-5eee-5d30-ad73-cef0a933573d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e4579a76-7eae-508b-b605-f6aa49421791" :question/math-academy-id "q-352757" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})={sec}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{{sec}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =0-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e39261b-18dc-5733-9697-439bb255e5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\ln(2)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e39261b-18dc-5733-9697-439bb255e5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\ln(2)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303014} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ec52e3-3172-5817-9d8b-f6d977c6d516" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "134020ff-4085-5cac-902e-babc37345e8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-362808" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}}\\frac{x}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}-{cot}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}}\\frac{x}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}-{cot}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}}\\frac{x}{({csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x)+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}}\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})\\,{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+(\\sqrt{e-1})^{2})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+(1)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+e-1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1)-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b85f5b77-adcc-5f3a-ac26-aeca80cb6b0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\tan (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095510} {:answer/id #uuid "270d5846-0eda-5c1b-b012-7d34d46cf1f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sec (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095511} {:answer/id #uuid "67d3a24a-4ea6-5077-8ee1-3c6b280ca8e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095512} {:answer/id #uuid "734b4c71-0e2a-55b8-a1c5-71df902ee0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\tan (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095513} {:answer/id #uuid "76de1b0f-7d81-565b-9186-9a8b04d73b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "734b4c71-0e2a-55b8-a1c5-71df902ee0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\tan (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095513} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c541591-f947-5bb0-83bf-cb48af5a8cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80d349d8-53d5-5ccb-8a77-300f5edef09d" :question/math-academy-id "q-49268" :question/problem "$\\int {tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & ={sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ {tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & ={sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\text{d}x & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\text{d}x-\\int 1\\cdot \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c8b83ae-7404-55d6-a950-0d46a83dd1af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303017} {:answer/id #uuid "e679cfa4-f400-5152-9ad2-e57c5cd09050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303018} {:answer/id #uuid "0c24d83a-967e-5ba4-9b86-7c5ec26c72a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303019} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a9610d-0636-532b-a80b-358c504d65e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303020} {:answer/id #uuid "b1acdfb2-6bc2-5f84-8bc2-1e1442e18197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c24d83a-967e-5ba4-9b86-7c5ec26c72a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303019} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb5ea80d-b788-58ce-aae1-1b363f933ce7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f125d694-dddf-5296-9b7a-4f3ef4027f35" :question/math-academy-id "q-49325" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We are using the identity\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =6-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb0d6b93-dbfb-5dbe-bc89-3f9e48f7f6f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303024} {:answer/id #uuid "7ed3d9ae-2e97-5009-b834-7cae8eb79b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303025} {:answer/id #uuid "d9747286-5341-5306-82dc-b77a4ae5e167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303026} {:answer/id #uuid "001494b8-9d22-5886-bc46-d1cc13086de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303027} {:answer/id #uuid "0909d7a3-2704-5782-be52-66358d672a4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "001494b8-9d22-5886-bc46-d1cc13086de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303027} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c547227-069f-5443-b066-444125ae8567" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "746c162e-1c21-5e8a-abb9-51161d5b4acf" :question/math-academy-id "q-49446" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.$ \nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}=\\frac{1}{-{sin}^{2}⁡x}=-{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "971ad7b9-ca5d-5b66-b8c1-b66d70160833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x - \\cot x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095756} {:answer/id #uuid "97859b41-7974-5d91-af6e-6d2908101b03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x - \\tan x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095757} {:answer/id #uuid "afa0db67-82af-5c4f-81e2-7c47a4774d4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\csc x + \\tan x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095758} {:answer/id #uuid "04c356ed-da2f-57ff-a442-e33763b86966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x - \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095759} {:answer/id #uuid "18275393-75a2-55a2-9dbb-5e9ef87ce4c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x + \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18275393-75a2-55a2-9dbb-5e9ef87ce4c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x + \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095760} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fcad329-096b-5878-ad00-aa6c2af14979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "549e92f3-8254-599c-8f33-a7787db1bdf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-51122" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c274f2bb-9344-51a6-a7f9-0fb0b7f0e920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303031} {:answer/id #uuid "cb53ef10-ddb8-558a-a661-06454e1d6910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303032} {:answer/id #uuid "8c32d7db-aec0-5a82-8305-441cb8292394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303033} {:answer/id #uuid "94bb518d-46d7-507e-9850-2013d1bca756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303034} {:answer/id #uuid "45bf8cf7-b3e9-59f7-b923-f2206715f06b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94bb518d-46d7-507e-9850-2013d1bca756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303034} :answer-field/id #uuid "85e159d3-7f85-5577-bbfb-430b24a2fdd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0fced1bb-0cac-510d-85df-b965aee24679" :question/math-academy-id "q-73513" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3({cot}^{2}⁡x+1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3({cot}^{2}⁡x+1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+3\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f15a6a1-f055-5f8f-bc84-175cbadea999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303038} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb1efd4-0c77-54ad-9680-e2bd69d9bd44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303039} {:answer/id #uuid "99528ec2-eeae-5e48-a844-17f9d6c49033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303040} {:answer/id #uuid "2460afa4-6468-558e-8b5f-d3969f947d88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303041} {:answer/id #uuid "4328d492-9546-55b3-b4a8-0219f86112ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99528ec2-eeae-5e48-a844-17f9d6c49033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303040} :answer-field/id #uuid "49df0dda-7518-5180-99f3-31434ba8ff99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f264faf5-d252-5bbb-b1de-13589dcbcfde" :question/math-academy-id "q-73518" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca8a09f9-6def-50a2-ad0a-01000b0c294f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303045} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b80f7e-9287-5c0a-ac4f-88345a12e1de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303046} {:answer/id #uuid "b058ab69-5cdc-5fb5-ae28-000956c9a043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303047} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff15703-e982-5a28-adb4-763d5ef0adfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303048} {:answer/id #uuid "918b9b52-606c-5d28-a3f5-ac3005d79074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b058ab69-5cdc-5fb5-ae28-000956c9a043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303047} :answer-field/id #uuid "434fc094-32c8-535b-8361-e66595bf9055" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01ad39ae-df60-544f-832a-8585e01a6563" :question/math-academy-id "q-73526" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
